  "content": {
    "id": "p12-q37-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "37",
    "prompt": "The ratio of the coefficients of $x^6$ and $x^7$ in $(2+ax)^{11}$ is $14:25$. Find the value of $a$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=5$.\n\nThe ordered coefficient ratio simplifies to $\\frac{14}{(5a)}$.",
      "worked": "$$T_k=\\binom{11}{k}2^{11-k}a^kx^k.$$\nThe required coefficient ratio is\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{[x^6]}{[x^7]}&=\\frac{\\binom{11}{6}2^5a^6}{\\binom{11}{7}2^4a^7}\\\\\\frac{[x^6]}{[x^7]}&=\\frac{462\\cdot2}{330a}\\\\\\frac{[x^6]}{[x^7]}&=\\frac{14}{5a}.\\end{align*}$$\nHence,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{14}{5a}&=\\frac{14}{25}\\\\5a&=25\\\\a&=5.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 80
  },
